<title>SPAIN: Santander charges higher after share split.</title>
<headline>Santander charges higher after share split.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in leading Spanish bank Santander rose strongly on Monday following its three-for-one share split, dealers said.</p>
<p>Shares in the group rose 140 pesetas, or 3.14 percent, to 4,605 pesetas, while the IBEX index of 35 leading shares was up 104.07 points, or 1.58 percent, to 6,720.51.</p>
<p>&quot;It's rising on the positive effect of the split,&quot; a Spanish bank dealer said.</p>
<p>On Saturday, Santander said it would cut its nominal share price from 750 pesetas to 250 pesetas in a share split, bringing the number of shares on the market to 479 milion from 159.7 million.</p>
<p>--Sharman Esarey, Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
